## Why This Is Asked
The goal is to assess practical pagination design and data modeling skills on a tiny API layer, including correctness and testability.

## Key Concepts
- Pagination parameters validation
- Indexed queries and ORDER BY performance
- Edge-case handling and test coverage

## Code Example

```javascript
function paginate(items, limit, offset) {
  if (limit <= 0 || offset < 0) throw new Error("Invalid pagination params");
  const total = items.length;
  const paged = items.slice(offset, offset + limit);
  return { total, items: paged };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test pagination with 10k+ records and caching?
- How would you adapt logic for distributed databases or replicas?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical debugging of per-tenant feature flags and zero-downtime rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes ConfigMaps and pod configuration propagation
- Environment variables vs mounted files for configuration delivery
- Canary deployments and rollback safety mechanisms
- Observability practices and latency budget management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Reads a per-tenant flag from environment variable with fallback to false
function isBetaEnabled(tenantId){
  const cfg = JSON.parse(process.env.TENANT_FLAGS || '{}');
  return !!cfg[tenantId]?.betaRoute;
}
```
